## Context

Decision [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) accepted subject-only merging.
The [review of #4471](/kb/incidents/4471-review) shows why identical words can conceal different mechanisms.
This proposal preserves the accepted decision and recommends replacing its rule; it does not claim the desk has adopted it.

## Proposed decision

Use subject text to search, then compare the underlying failure before merging.
For the date reports, look up tenant locale and booking form and retain the channel.
Do not classify by browser locale or intake tag alone. Use the executable cause rules for the export's grouping,
and retain contradictory report bodies as uncertainty requiring investigation.

Merge only when the cause matches. Keep parser and booking-v3 hint work in separate issues, with report IDs
and one count per unique report. When tenant details or the mechanism are missing, leave the cause unplaced
and request original input, displayed hint, stored timestamp and timezone evidence.

<DedupeExplorer />

## Consequences

Triage takes a lookup and a reading of the report rather than a subject match alone.
Engineering receives a thread per mechanism with an auditable count. Support keeps conflicting evidence visible
and revisits old guidance when rendered components disagree with prose.

